# Generated image ownership

Run image emission after publication filtering and indexing, before the index module is serialized. Store only Svartz-generated files under each vault's mounted `__svartz/` path. This keeps rebuild cleanup and multi-vault isolation under the existing artifact pipeline.

Pass only public title, description, and site title to the theme's SVG preview template. Encrypted or hidden notes use the configured site fallback, and unpublished notes never reach the emitter. A note's explicit image may retain a published attachment, but an excluded attachment must fail rather than leak through.

Host apps own their favicon until `discovery.favicon.enabled` is true. The favicon source path resolves from the config directory. SvelteKit's static prerenderer crawls local icon links; use an absolute public URL when available, and an inlined icon when no `site.url` exists. See `docs/images.md` for the consumer contract.
